{{!
    @template minilessonitem_smartframe/smartframe

    A widget item. The iframe has no src here: the item's JS sets it once it is listening for the widget's
    messages, so the widget's first message can not be missed.

    The sandbox lets the widget run scripts but not keep Moodle's origin, so it runs in an opaque origin of
    its own and can not reach Moodle's cookies or pages. Never add allow-same-origin: the widget is served
    from Moodle's site. (widget.php sends the same sandbox as a policy header too, which also covers a widget
    page opened in a tab of its own.) allow-forms is there because a form submit in a sandbox without it is
    dropped before the submit event, which breaks widgets that handle submit in JS.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "uniqueid": "item1",
        "widgeturl": "https://school.example.org/mod/minilesson/item/smartframe/widget.php/12/0123/index.html?lang=en&parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fschool.example.org",
        "widgettitle": "Greetings"
    }
}}
{{> mod_minilesson/questionheader}}
<div class="minilessonitem_smartframe_widget">
    {{#widgeturl}}
        <iframe class="minilessonitem_smartframe_frame"
                title="{{widgettitle}}"
                sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms"
                referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
                loading="lazy"
                style="display:block;width:100%;height:360px;border:0;"></iframe>
    {{/widgeturl}}
    {{^widgeturl}}
        <div class="alert alert-info">{{#str}}widgetnotavailable, minilessonitem_smartframe{{/str}}</div>
    {{/widgeturl}}
</div>
{{> mod_minilesson/questionfooter}}
